<h2>How a 1968–70 Charger VIN is laid out</h2>
<p>Chrysler’s 13-character VIN, for example <strong>XS29L8B100001</strong>, reads like this:</p>
<div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="w-full text-sm text-left text-silver-300 border border-white/10"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-silver-200"><tr><th class="p-3">Position</th><th class="p-3">Example</th><th class="p-3">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">1</td><td class="p-3">X</td><td class="p-3">Car line: X = Dodge Charger</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">2</td><td class="p-3">S</td><td class="p-3">Price class: P = Premium, S = Special (R/T), X = Fast Top (1969 Charger 500), H = High (1970)</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">3–4</td><td class="p-3">29</td><td class="p-3">Body: 29 = 2-door sports hardtop</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">5</td><td class="p-3">L</td><td class="p-3">Engine (year-specific; see below)</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">6</td><td class="p-3">8</td><td class="p-3">Model year: 8 = 1968, 9 = 1969, 0 = 1970</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">7</td><td class="p-3">B</td><td class="p-3">Assembly plant</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">8–13</td><td class="p-3">100001</td><td class="p-3">Plant sequence, starting at 100001 each year</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Charger prefixes</h2>
<div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="w-full text-sm text-left text-silver-300 border border-white/10"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-silver-200"><tr><th class="p-3">Prefix</th><th class="p-3">Years</th><th class="p-3">Model</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">XP29</td><td class="p-3">1968–69</td><td class="p-3">Charger</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">XS29</td><td class="p-3">1968–70</td><td class="p-3">Charger R/T</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">XX29</td><td class="p-3">1969</td><td class="p-3">Charger 500 (Fast Top class)</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">XH29</td><td class="p-3">1970</td><td class="p-3">Charger</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">XP29</td><td class="p-3">1970</td><td class="p-3">Charger 500</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Engine codes</h2>
<div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="w-full text-sm text-left text-silver-300 border border-white/10"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-silver-200"><tr><th class="p-3">Code</th><th class="p-3">1968</th><th class="p-3">1969</th><th class="p-3">1970</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">318 V8</td><td class="p-3">318 V8</td><td class="p-3">—</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">G</td><td class="p-3">383 V8</td><td class="p-3">383 V8</td><td class="p-3">318 V8</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">H</td><td class="p-3">383 V8 high performance</td><td class="p-3">383 V8 high performance</td><td class="p-3">—</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">J</td><td class="p-3">426 Hemi</td><td class="p-3">426 Hemi</td><td class="p-3">—</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">L</td><td class="p-3">440 V8 high performance</td><td class="p-3">440 V8 high performance</td><td class="p-3">383 V8</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">M</td><td class="p-3">Special-order V8</td><td class="p-3">Special-order V8 (used on 440 Six Pack cars)</td><td class="p-3">—</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">N</td><td class="p-3">—</td><td class="p-3">—</td><td class="p-3">383 V8 high performance</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">R</td><td class="p-3">—</td><td class="p-3">—</td><td class="p-3">426 Hemi</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">U</td><td class="p-3">—</td><td class="p-3">—</td><td class="p-3">440 V8 4-barrel high performance</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">V</td><td class="p-3">—</td><td class="p-3">—</td><td class="p-3">440 Six Pack</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>1968–69 codes come from Dodge’s factory VIN bulletins. 1970 codes come from Charger club registries, so the decoder marks them “Likely” rather than “Documented.”</p>
<h2>Plants</h2>
<div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="w-full text-sm text-left text-silver-300 border border-white/10"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-silver-200"><tr><th class="p-3">Code</th><th class="p-3">Plant</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">A</td><td class="p-3">Lynch Road (Detroit), Michigan</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">B</td><td class="p-3">Hamtramck, Michigan</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">E</td><td class="p-3">Los Angeles, California</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">G</td><td class="p-3">St. Louis, Missouri</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>All 1970 Chargers were built in St. Louis. The decoder warns you if a 1970 Charger shows another plant letter.</p>
<h2>Hemi and R/T clones</h2>
<p>Few classics are cloned as often as Hemi and 440 Chargers. A correct VIN plate is only the start. Match it to the fender tag, the partial VIN stamped on the engine and transmission, and the broadcast sheet. Inspect the plate rivets, and get documentation before paying a premium.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What does XS29 mean on a Charger VIN?</h3><p>X is the Charger car line, S is the Special price class used for the R/T, and 29 is the 2-door sports hardtop body.</p><h3>What is the Hemi code in a Charger VIN?</h3><p>The fifth character J means a 426 Hemi on 1968–69 cars; on 1970 cars the Hemi code is R.</p><h3>Where were 1970 Chargers built?</h3><p>All 1970 Chargers were assembled in St. Louis, plant code G.</p>
